{"lines":[{"t":"Reading","h":0.022600613080846266,"c":1,"w":0.074685611724853551,"y":0.050902218186171577,"x":0.83822418281705779},{"c":1,"t":"READING PASSAGE 3","w":0.26124567667643228,"x":0.18858131381660864,"y":0.10174418576058963,"h":0.017570019769368228},{"c":1,"x":0.18858131196857528,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading","w":0.71453287760416662,"h":0.018913657453362154,"y":0.1409883721211922},{"y":0.16130160975353758,"t":"Passage 3 below.","x":0.18858131268436812,"w":0.14359862009684243,"h":0.016095171448565537,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.45674738566080725,"x":0.32179931746092355,"y":0.19622093047560774,"t":"Book review: The World of Sugar by","h":0.026312309516068555},{"y":0.22813156021530756,"t":"Ulbe Bosma","x":0.47404844319011696,"w":0.15397923787434897,"h":0.020414951049505636,"c":1},{"y":0.27906976716018228,"w":0.71972320556640623,"c":1,"h":0.01744186102384615,"t":"Ulbe Bosma's The World of Sugar is a genuinely global history. Bosma discusses all the sugar-","x":0.18858130369665502},{"y":0.29636109154261026,"h":0.019045885164809429,"t":"growing places of the world, beginning with Cuba and Java, the largest exporters of the early","w":0.71280278523763041,"x":0.18858130614914131,"c":1},{"h":0.019046902239447827,"t":"20th century. But this is a history not just of cane sugar but also of beet sugar, an equally","x":0.18858131074338169,"c":1,"y":0.315255423308472,"w":0.68339101155598958},{"h":0.01899401102139453,"c":1,"t":"important form of traded sugar over the last hundred years. Beet sugar is grown mainly in","x":0.18685121045220351,"y":0.33275017498196413,"w":0.69204152425130216},{"y":0.35164450689559068,"w":0.71972315470377612,"c":1,"x":0.18858133653219492,"h":0.017541539010007101,"t":"Europe and the United States. It has also been massively subsidised and sold at artificially low"},{"t":"prices on world markets, threatening the livelihood of producers of cane sugar.","w":0.60553634643554677,"y":0.37053883819748712,"h":0.017542557419389149,"x":0.18858130785219468,"c":1},{"t":"Bosma's discussion of the sugar market in Britain gives a sense of the book's range.","c":1,"w":0.64532872517903639,"x":0.18858131728937441,"y":0.40552325565604064,"h":0.018899417741053304},{"c":1,"w":0.65063471476236989,"h":0.020723212090632992,"x":0.18852138703662774,"y":0.42377581099096073,"t":"The sweet-toothed British first bought cane sugar from their own slavery-dependent"},{"y":0.44331395320570377,"x":0.18685121266139088,"w":0.68512110392252601,"h":0.017497803465814421,"c":1,"t":"colonial plantations. Following the abolition of slavery in the British Empire, cane sugar"},{"y":0.46220930204341237,"w":0.64013839721679688,"c":1,"t":"was imported to Britain from places which retained the practice, such as Cuba and","x":0.18685121652472494,"h":0.017496786391176133},{"w":0.69031143188476562,"h":0.018949257067819802,"y":0.47965116281694242,"t":"Brazil. Towards the end of the 19th century, the British started to import beet sugar from","x":0.1885813081925653,"c":1},{"x":0.18685121010736794,"y":0.49999999971824582,"h":0.017494751574527512,"w":0.69204152425130205,"c":1,"t":"continental Europe. Only in the 20th century was there a move to develop a national beet"},{"c":1,"h":0.019864502113294269,"x":0.18674347852928042,"t":"sugar industry.","y":0.51550379521666045,"w":0.11786252339680992},{"w":0.69377161661783848,"x":0.18685121582698733,"h":0.018999097061958015,"t":"The book provides a global labour history, investigating the wide range of labour regimes","y":0.55377906979586533,"c":1},{"x":0.18685122215268335,"t":"associated with growing sugar. Contrary to popular belief, cane sugar production was never","h":0.017598499861357531,"w":0.71107264200846354,"y":0.57267441832264354,"c":1},{"x":0.18512111564254297,"y":0.59011627923975107,"h":0.017441859689102501,"c":1,"t":"just restricted to large, dedicated plantations owned by rich men. For example, in Java, a","w":0.68512110392252612},{"x":0.18685121644115563,"c":1,"y":0.60901162762545313,"t":"huge exporter of sugar in the early 20th century, sugar cane was grown together with rice in","w":0.70934254964192711,"h":0.01744186102384615},{"y":0.62790697645986604,"h":0.01744186102384615,"w":0.44463668823242186,"c":1,"t":"an extraordinarily labour-intensive way by small farmers.","x":0.18685120597766683},{"w":0.64186848958333331,"t":"The World of Sugar is also a story of similarity and continuity in sugar cultivation.","c":1,"y":0.66270118979233028,"h":0.018984856682277451,"x":0.18685122234895354},{"h":0.017532386005633893,"x":0.18685121645392608,"y":0.68159552124786427,"t":"For example, imported labour has been used for much large-scale production. German beet","c":1,"w":0.70934254964192711},{"x":0.18685121010618294,"t":"fields employed Polish workers; Mexicans and many others, including Sicilians, were vital","h":0.018986890831554248,"w":0.69204152425130205,"y":0.70048985332107783,"c":1},{"x":0.1850728060845076,"w":0.67659627278645829,"h":0.020658045902879563,"t":"to US sugar production. Cane cutting, Bosma shows, remains a poorly paid and brutal","c":1,"y":0.71728195334530875},{"x":0.18685119865768493,"y":0.73687893645617575,"c":1,"h":0.017494751574527623,"t":"business to this day in many places in the world. But as well as this, the book is about the","w":0.6885813395182292},{"x":0.18685121010986394,"h":0.017494751574527623,"w":0.69204152425130205,"c":1,"t":"continuity of the use of traditional methods on small farms. In the mid 20th-century, this","y":0.75577326821903823},{"h":0.017506957804931389,"x":0.18685120456732876,"y":0.77325581367097507,"c":1,"t":"type of sugar production dominated in South Asia and Latin America.","w":0.55190312703450528},{"y":0.8093589171512342,"t":"This is also a history of capitalists and sugar dynasties, as well as corporations that in","w":0.6627223205566406,"c":1,"h":0.020220611711079028,"x":0.18680910371878365},{"h":0.019011302624990067,"t":"some cases have remained influential over very long periods. Great firms and great interests","w":0.70761245727539057,"y":0.82703488374492029,"c":1,"x":0.18512110689205211},{"t":"have had profound influence on the policies of states. In many places - not just the British","w":0.69550170898437513,"x":0.18685122154565903,"h":0.017556797131697888,"c":1,"y":0.84738372064869283},{"x":0.18685121608630481,"w":0.6557093302408854,"t":"Caribbean but Cuba and the Philippines too - a powerful sugar bourgeoisie played a","h":0.019063176768405077,"c":1,"y":0.86337209281810445},{"x":0.18512110375091406,"t":"major role in politics and their interests were consequently protected by trade barriers and","w":0.6989619445800781,"h":0.017608671275112897,"c":1,"y":0.88372092995095131},{"t":"subsidies. In the battle for control of the industry, it was inevitably the poor countries which","w":0.71280278523763019,"h":0.019061141951756566,"y":0.90116279072376848,"x":0.1851210987098322,"c":1},{"x":0.18512111018018801,"c":1,"w":0.64705881754557293,"y":0.92005813925289193,"h":0.01744186102384615,"t":"came off worse. All this is explored by Bosma with wonderful subtlety and control."},{"w":0.022491348584492976,"h":0.014534884186538477,"t":"25","c":1,"y":0.9549418601717502,"x":0.88235294154541222}],"w":2400,"h":2857}